AB  - With the increasing integration of urban renewal and smart city development, communities as the basic spatial units of residents’ daily lives, face a structural disconnect between the optimization of physical space and the application of smart technologies in their renewal. To address these issues, this paper constructs an integrated smart community space renewal technology path encompassing “spatial assessment-problem diagnosis-solution generation.” This path aims to achieve intelligent auxiliary decision-making from problem identification to strategy output through the synergy of multi-source data fusion and planning knowledge enhancement, thereby integrating smart technologies into community space renewal. The framework first integrates multi-source spatial data to construct a four-dimensional evaluation index system covering space utilization intensity, resident demand intensity, time fluctuation index, and existing smart level. Based on grid units, a comprehensive renewal priority index is calculated to identify high-priority renovation spaces. Next, AI visual recognition and retrieval-enhanced generative large language models (LLMs) are introduced to perform image semantic analysis and problem cause diagnosis for typical spaces. Finally, relying on a localized knowledge base in the planning field, targeted renewal strategies are automatically generated, and AI text-based image generation technology is coupled to achieve rapid visualization and generation of renovation solutions. Subsequently, using the Huayuan Road community in Nanjing, China as a case study, public activity spaces, parking spaces, residential roads, and community entrances were identified as high-priority space types. Smart transformation strategies and visual solutions were generated for each type of space characteristic. The results show that this framework can support the systematic nature of community space problem diagnosis. While reducing reliance on individual experience, it enhances the traceability and transparency of planning decisions, providing a reusable methodological framework and operational path for smart community upgrades oriented towards residents’ needs.
